WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.918
Today is about noticing. A reader who takes it in knows at once when a sentence makes no sense.

2
00:00:06.368 --> 00:00:13.180
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.260
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:22.664
Every sentence on today's page has one word that does not fit. Your child reads it out loud.

5
00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:24.644
The dog had a nap on the sun.

6
00:00:25.444 --> 00:00:29.169
Ask: does that make sense? Wait. Let your child laugh at it.

7
00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:35.147
Your child crosses out the word that does not fit. Then circles the picture of something that would.

8
00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:37.021
Then say the rule together.

9
00:00:37.471 --> 00:00:40.263
If it makes no sense, I stop, and I read it again.

10
00:00:41.063 --> 00:00:47.702
That rule is for every book. Most of the time, a sentence that makes no sense means a word was read wrong.

11
00:00:48.152 --> 00:00:55.774
For job two, press play on the listening track and step away. The voice reads each silly sentence just as it is printed.

12
00:00:56.224 --> 00:01:01.041
Then your child crosses out the silly word, and draws a line to the picture that fits.

13
00:01:01.491 --> 00:01:05.328
At the end, your child says each sentence to you, the way it makes sense.
